-- Growth Q and A: carry the model's answer as well as the rewrite.
--
-- The first import took only `better` -- the version a person actually says -- and threw
-- away `aiBetter`, the answer the model wrote. Luke's screen shows both, one under the
-- other, because that IS the lesson: the rewrite is shorter, splits the long sentence up
-- and adds what only somebody who has been on the calls would know. With one of them the
-- row is just an answer; with both it shows the edit.
--
-- Also brings `bullets` where somebody has written them by hand (one question has). The
-- rest derive from the answer at render time, split at sentence ends and capped at six,
-- which is what his qaBullets does and what grQaPoints already did.
--
-- Read out of the artifact's own database, not retyped.

update growth_settings set value = $json${"items": [{"a": "No guarantee, and say so. What he promises is daily work and honesty. Work starts in 2 to 5 days after payment, ads usually go live in about 7 to 10 days, and the client will know in month one or two. If it is not working after about two weeks they say so and pivot.", "aiBetter": "I will not promise a number, and anyone who does is guessing. What I can promise is daily work and full honesty. You will see the first ads live in about a week, real data in month one, and if it is not working by week two I will tell you and change the plan. We only keep clients that make money, so I have every reason to make it work.", "better": "I will not promise a number. Anyone who does is guessing. What I can promise is daily work and full honesty. You see the first ads live in about a week and real data in month one. If it is not working by week two, I will tell you and change the plan. We only keep clients who make money, so I have every reason to make it work. \n we have a great team", "bullets": ["I will not promise a number.", "Anyone who does is guessing.", "What I can promise is daily work and full honesty.", "You see the first ads live in about a week and real data in month one.", "If it is not working by week two, I will tell you and change the plan.", "We only keep clients who make money, so I have every reason to make it work."], "calls": 37, "feel": "Will I waste my money?", "id": "results", "n": 65, "q": "Can you guarantee results? How fast will I see them?", "theme": "Results and timeline", "tricks": ["Do not promise ROAS", "Give the timeline in days", "Say we only keep clients by making them money", "Promise honesty and effort instead"], "why": "Honest beats hopeful. Say there is no guarantee, then show the plan, the timeline and the exit. Trust goes up when you do not promise."}, {"a": "Google Ads is $1,500 a month (up to $15,000 ad spend, about 10% of spend above that). Meta Ads is $1,800 to $2,000. SEO is $2,400 to $2,500. Google plus Meta together is $2,500 to $3,000. Everything (Rocket Fuel) is $5,000. Ad spend is on top and paid straight to Google or Meta. No setup fee.", "aiBetter": "Here is how it works. Our Google Ads management is $1,500 a month. That covers daily management, building the campaigns, perfect conversion tracking and the small landing page fixes. There is no setup fee, and your ad spend goes straight to Google from your own card. Does that range work for you?", "better": "Our Google Ads management is $1,500 a month. That covers daily management, building the campaigns, proper conversion tracking and small landing page fixes. There is no setup fee. Your ad spend goes straight to Google from your own card. Does that work for you?", "calls": 50, "feel": "Is this fair, and will I be surprised later?", "id": "price", "n": 62, "q": "What does it cost?", "theme": "Pricing and budget", "tricks": ["Say what is included before the price", "Close with a question, not silence", "Use the same numbers every call"], "why": "Most people want one number and a reason it is fair. Lead with the outcome, give the price, then say what is included and that there is no setup fee."}, {"a": "A Stripe payment link on autopay, a short contract confirming they own the accounts, and a 15 to 30 minute onboarding form that goes to the team. Matthew Overbay (general manager) then calls. The team audits and researches competitors, presents a plan in about a week, then launches and adjusts every week or two.", "aiBetter": "Five steps. One, I send a payment link. Two, you fill a 15 minute form. Three, Matthew, our general manager, calls you. Four, in about a week we show you the full plan before anything goes live. Five, we launch and adjust every week. You just do steps one and two.", "better": "Five simple steps. One, I send you a payment link. Two, you fill out a 15 minute form. Three, Matthew, our general manager, calls you. Four, in about a week we show you the full plan before anything goes live. Five, we launch and adjust every week. You only do steps one and two.", "calls": 47, "feel": "How hard is it to get started, and what will I have to do?", "id": "onboard", "n": 53, "q": "What happens after I say yes? How does onboarding work?", "theme": "How it works", "tricks": ["Number the steps", "Name a real person (Matthew)", "Show the plan before going live", "Make step one tiny"], "why": "Make it feel like five easy steps. People say yes faster when the next step is small and clear."}, {"a": "Google Ads is buyer intent and the fastest predictable way to get leads and calls. Meta suits products and trust based offers, not usually B2B. SEO is slow, three to six months, and also now covers AI search and Maps. Start with the channel that fits the buyer, test small, then add.", "aiBetter": "Before I say, how do people find you today? If they search for what you sell, Google Ads is the fastest and most predictable. If it is a product people discover, Meta is strong. SEO is the long game, three to six months. I would start with one, prove it, then add the next.", "better": "It depends on how people find you today. If they search for what you sell, Google Ads is the fastest and most predictable. If people find you by browsing, Meta is strong. SEO is the long game, about three to six months. I would start with one, prove it works, then add the next.", "calls": 35, "feel": "What is the right first move for my situation?", "id": "channel", "n": 45, "q": "Should I do Google Ads, Meta or SEO?", "theme": "Services and fit", "tricks": ["Ask how customers find them", "Explain Google as buyer intent", "Say SEO is the long game", "Start with one channel"], "why": "Ask first. How do their customers find them today? Then recommend, and start small."}, {"a": "No annual contract. It is a three month minimum, paid one month at a time, with a 10 day exit. The contract says the client owns every account and asset, and ReachGiant never holds anything hostage.", "aiBetter": "No long contract. It is three months because the first month is setup and testing, and you only see real data in month two. You pay one month at a time, and if it is not for you, email me in the first week and we part ways. You own every account, always.", "better": "No long contract. It is three months because the first month is setup and testing, and real data shows up in month two. You pay one month at a time. If it is not for you, email me in the first week and we part ways. You own every account, always.", "calls": 42, "feel": "What if I get stuck and cannot get out?", "id": "contract", "n": 44, "q": "Is there a contract? How long do I have to commit?", "theme": "Contracts and commitment", "tricks": ["Explain why three months", "Offer the 10 day exit up front", "Say the client owns the accounts"], "why": "Say the exit before they ask. It removes the fear and it sounds confident."}, {"a": "Bare minimum is $1,000 a month in ad spend, $1,500 is typical, and $2,500 to $3,000 is a better start. Start light, test for the first month or two, then scale only when ROAS or profit on ad spend is there. Ad spend stays in the client's own account on their own card.", "aiBetter": "Good question. What is a new customer worth to you? If a sale is $2,000, then $1,500 a month is enough to test, and $2,500 gives you faster learning. We start light, watch the numbers for the first month, and only raise it when it pays back.", "better": "It depends on what a new customer is worth to you. If a sale is $2,000, then $1,500 a month is enough to start testing. $2,500 gets you answers faster. We start light, watch the numbers for the first month, and only raise it when it pays back.", "calls": 32, "feel": "How much will this really cost me in total?", "id": "adspend", "n": 39, "q": "How much should I spend on ads? Is my budget enough?", "theme": "Tracking and ad spend", "tricks": ["Ask what a customer is worth first", "Say start light and prove it", "Remind them the spend stays in their account"], "why": "Do not give a number cold. Ask what a customer is worth, then work backwards. It makes your number feel earned."}, {"a": "They never niched. About 45 to 50 clients across ecommerce and service businesses, roughly 4 years as ReachGiant. Name the closest real example (painters, movers, flooring, Apple watch seller, scooters). If there is no exact match, say so and explain the plan is the same: seasonality, locations, keywords, competitors.", "aiBetter": "We have not done exactly that, and I would rather say so. We have done painters, movers and flooring companies, and the plan is the same: your seasons, your locations, your keywords and your competitors. I can send you a short video from a client with a similar setup. Would that help?", "better": "We have not done exactly your type of business, and I would rather be honest about that. We have worked with painters, movers and flooring companies. The plan is the same: your seasons, your areas, your keywords and your competitors. I can send you a short video from a client with a similar setup. Would that help?", "calls": 30, "feel": "Will you understand my business?", "id": "industry", "n": 33, "q": "Have you worked with a business like mine?", "theme": "Proof and experience", "tricks": ["Be honest about no exact match", "Name the closest real example", "Offer a video or a reference", "Say the plan is the same every time"], "why": "Do not pretend to match exactly. Say what is close, then prove the plan travels. Then offer a real reference."}, {"a": "A team of 10 to 12, US based and salaried, with Luke as owner and Matthew Overbay as general manager in New York. About four people touch an account: strategist, Google and Meta techs, designer, and a developer for tracking.", "aiBetter": "You get a team, not one freelancer. We are 12 people, all in the US. Matthew Overbay, our general manager in New York, leads your account, with a Google tech, a Meta tech, a designer and a developer for tracking. You will talk to them directly.", "better": "You get a team, not one freelancer. We are 12 people, all in the US. Matthew Overbay, our general manager in New York, leads your account. A Google specialist, a Meta specialist, a designer and a developer for tracking all work on it. You talk to them directly.", "calls": 26, "feel": "Am I buying a real team or one person?", "id": "team", "n": 32, "q": "Who will actually work on my account? Where is your team?", "theme": "Who does the work", "tricks": ["Give the team size", "Name the general manager", "List the roles"], "why": "Give numbers and names. A real team beats a promise."}, {"a": "Reviews are public: hundreds of Google reviews, Fiverr Pro agency, Upwork top 1%. The team is US based with salaried specialists. Accounts stay in the client's name. The first two months decide whether they keep the client, so results come first. Admit that not every campaign works.", "aiBetter": "That is a fair worry, and honestly it happens a lot in this industry. Three things protect you. Your accounts stay in your name, so we can never hold them. You can leave on 10 days notice. And you can read our reviews online first. We only keep clients by making them money, so I would rather earn your trust slowly.", "better": "That is a fair worry, and it happens a lot in this industry. Three things protect you. Your accounts stay in your name, so we can never take them. You can leave on 10 days notice. And you can read our reviews online first. We only keep clients by making them money, so I would rather earn your trust slowly.", "calls": 26, "feel": "I have been burned before. Why would you be different?", "id": "trust", "n": 32, "q": "Why should I trust you? Past agencies burned me.", "theme": "Trust and past agencies", "tricks": ["Agree before you answer", "Give three clear protections", "Point to public reviews", "Never sound defensive"], "why": "When someone says they were burned, agree first. Never defend. Then show proof and the exit."}, {"a": "Small landing page fixes (nav, CTAs, duplicate pages) are included in Google Ads management. Full websites and branding are separate quotes: nothing under $10,000, average about $25,000, websites alone from $10,000 and a $1,500 workshop is available.", "aiBetter": "Small landing page fixes are included in your management. A full new site is a separate project. Most start around $10,000 and the average is about $25,000, so I would not start there unless the site is the problem. Let us run ads first, see what the numbers say, then decide.", "better": "Small landing page fixes are included in your management. A full new site is a separate project. Most start around $10,000, and the average is about $25,000. I would not start there unless the site is the real problem. Let us run ads first, see what the numbers say, then decide.", "calls": 29, "feel": "Will my website hold this back?", "id": "web", "n": 31, "q": "Do you build websites and landing pages? What does it cost?", "theme": "Services and fit", "tricks": ["Say small fixes are included", "Be clear on project prices", "Suggest ads first if the budget is tight"], "why": "Do not market a site that does not convert. Say it kindly, then offer a quote or a smaller step."}, {"a": "The $1,500 is built for real work by a US team, so it does not go far below. For small or new businesses Luke has dropped Google Ads to $1,000 to $1,300 and the vault to $1,500 to $2,000. The bare minimum ad spend is $1,000. Under about $1,000 total, point them to a trusted freelancer instead.", "aiBetter": "I hear you, and I want this to work at your size. Normally it is $1,500. For a new business I can do $1,000 if we start this week, because I want to prove what a real team does with a small budget. I would just ask you to keep that between us. Fair?", "better": "I hear you, and I want this to work at your size. Normally it is $1,500 a month. For a new business, I can do $1,000 if we start this week. I want to show you what a real team does with a smaller budget. I would just ask you to keep that between us. Fair?", "calls": 26, "feel": "I want this to work, but I am afraid I cannot afford it.", "id": "lower", "n": 27, "q": "Can you do it cheaper? My budget is small.", "theme": "Pricing and budget", "tricks": ["Give a reason for the discount", "Tie it to deciding today", "Ask them to keep it private", "Offer one discount only, then hold it"], "why": "The best deals so far came when the discount had a reason and a deadline. Never drop the price without something in return."}, {"a": "Google Tag Manager and Analytics on every account, conversion API through Stape for Meta, and a bot blocker (Clixie) for spam. They track calls, forms and drop offs, and report ROAS or profit on ad spend. For service businesses the client reports closes, or they use a lead to close ratio.", "aiBetter": "Tracking is included, and we set it up first. We track calls, forms and sales in Google and Meta, we block bot traffic, and we show it in plain words: what you spent, what you made, and what we will do next. If it is not tracked, we do not scale it.", "better": "We set tracking up first, before anything else. We track calls, forms and sales in Google and Meta, and we block bot traffic. Then we show you in plain words: what you spent, what you made, and what we will do next. If it is not tracked, we do not scale it.", "calls": 21, "feel": "How will I know it is working and not made up?", "id": "tracking", "n": 24, "q": "How do you track results and make sure leads are real?", "theme": "Tracking and ad spend", "tricks": ["Say tracking is included", "Mention bot blocking", "Promise plain words", "Only scale what is proven"], "why": "Tracking is a selling point. Say it is included and that you will explain it simply."}, {"a": "Current answer: they only do Google and Meta, SEO, plus web and branding. They no longer offer cold email or LinkedIn, do not do CRM or automations, do not make UGC, and do not do one time audits or consulting. Training is rare and priced separately. Refer out cleanly.", "aiBetter": "That one is not our thing, and I would rather tell you than waste your money. We do Google Ads, Meta, SEO, and websites. For that, I can point you to someone good. If you want the ads side, I am happy to help.", "better": "That is not something we do, and I would rather tell you now than waste your money. We do Google Ads, Meta ads, SEO and websites. For the rest, I can point you to someone good. If you want the ads side, I am happy to help.", "calls": 17, "feel": "Can you solve my exact problem?", "id": "notdo", "n": 19, "q": "Can you also do [cold email, CRM, UGC, one time audit, training]?", "theme": "Services and fit", "tricks": ["Say no quickly and kindly", "Say what you do best", "Offer a referral"], "why": "A fast, kind no builds trust. Say what you do best, then point them somewhere good."}, {"a": "Custom to the client. Email replies usually within a couple of hours, a booking link for calls, a strategy call after payment and a second one a week later. Reports are short Loom videos explaining spend, what is working and the plan, not big PDFs.", "aiBetter": "You choose how involved you are. Most clients get a short Loom video from us, ten minutes, showing what we did, what worked and what is next. No giant PDFs. Email us any time and we reply within a couple of hours, and we can jump on a call whenever you want.", "better": "You pick how involved you want to be. Most clients get a short Loom video from us, about ten minutes, showing what we did, what worked and what is next. No giant PDFs. Email us anytime and we reply within a couple of hours. We can also hop on a call whenever you want.", "calls": 17, "feel": "Will I be left in the dark?", "id": "comms", "n": 18, "q": "How will we communicate and how will you report?", "theme": "How it works", "tricks": ["Offer Loom videos", "Give a reply time", "Let them choose how involved to be"], "why": "Sell the easy part: you will always know what is happening, in plain words."}, {"a": "Google Ads, Meta Ads, SEO, plus web and branding, with about 12 people and 45 to 50 clients across ecommerce and service businesses. They say honestly when someone is not a fit.", "aiBetter": "Great question. We run Google and Meta ads and SEO for businesses that already make sales and want more. Before I say if you are a fit, tell me a little about your business and what a good result would look like in a year. I will tell you straight if we are the right team or someone else is.", "better": "We run Google and Meta ads and SEO for businesses that already make sales and want more. Tell me a bit about your business and what a good result looks like in a year. Then I will tell you straight if we are the right team or if someone else is a better fit.", "calls": 10, "feel": "Will you actually understand my business?", "id": "fit", "n": 11, "q": "What do you do, and am I a good fit?", "theme": "Services and fit", "tricks": ["Ask before you pitch", "Promise a straight answer", "Make it about their goal"], "why": "Curiosity beats a pitch. Ask first, then answer with honesty."}, {"a": "Manual outreach and guest posts for backlinks, with a plan, workbooks and monthly reporting. Cold email only makes sense when the offer, market and reputation line up, and it starts at around $4,500.", "aiBetter": "Fair to ask, because there is a lot of junk out there. Everything is done by hand: we pick real sites in your field, write real content, and send one to one messages, nothing automated. You see every link we earn each month. And I will tell you early if your offer is not ready for it. Want me to show you an example?", "better": "Fair question, there is a lot of junk out there. Everything is done by hand. We pick real sites in your field, write real content, and send one to one messages. Nothing is automated. You see every link we earn each month. If your offer is not ready for it, I will tell you early. Want me to show you an example?", "calls": 7, "feel": "Show me it is real and not spammy.", "id": "outbound", "n": 11, "q": "How do link building and cold email actually work?", "theme": "How it works", "tricks": ["Agree there is junk out there", "Show the work visibly", "Promise an early honest answer"], "why": "Acknowledge the distrust, make the work visible, and promise honesty."}, {"a": "An in house designer and video editor turn the client's photos and footage into ads. They do not film new content or make UGC, and they avoid throwaway AI images.", "aiBetter": "You do not need to be a creator. Send me whatever you already have: product photos, a phone video, even screenshots. Our designer and editor turn that into ads, and I will tell you exactly which extra content would help most. Does that feel doable?", "better": "You do not need to be a creator. Send us what you already have, like product photos, a phone video or screenshots. Our designer and editor turn that into ads. I will also tell you which extra content would help most. Does that feel doable?", "calls": 10, "feel": "Will I have to create everything myself?", "id": "creative", "n": 10, "q": "Who makes the ads, videos and images?", "theme": "Who does the work", "tricks": ["Make their part feel small", "Name the exact thing you do not do", "Offer a clear next step"], "why": "People fear extra work. Show them the first step is tiny, then be clear about the one thing you do not do."}, {"a": "No free audits, since a proper review takes five to ten hours. Work starts once they sign. Luke offers a quick look or a short overview, and the plan comes in the first week.", "aiBetter": "I understand wanting proof first. A real audit takes our team five to ten hours, so I do not give it away free, but here is what I do: I will take a quick look right now and tell you the two biggest things I see. And in your first week you see the full plan before anything goes live, with a 10 day exit if you are not happy. Fair?", "better": "I get it, you want to see something first. A real audit takes our team five to ten hours, so we do not give it away free. What I can do is take a quick look now and tell you the two biggest things I see. And in week one you see the full plan before anything goes live. If you are not happy, you can leave with 10 days notice.", "calls": 7, "feel": "I want to see proof before I commit.", "id": "audit", "n": 7, "q": "Can I get an audit, a plan or a quote first?", "theme": "Services and fit", "tricks": ["Give a small taste now", "Explain why not, kindly", "Lower risk with the exit"], "why": "Respect the request, say why not, then give something real on the spot and lower the risk."}, {"a": "They can run ads in other languages with AI translation and target by radius, zip code or country. Luke advised focusing on the words people use to search rather than only locations.", "aiBetter": "Yes. We have run campaigns across countries. We translate carefully and target by country, city or radius. Often the smartest move is to start with the one market that has the best customers, prove it works, then add the next. Which country is your best customer in today?", "better": "Yes. We have run campaigns in other countries. We translate carefully and target by country, city or radius. Often the smartest move is to start with the one market that has your best customers, prove it works, then add the next. Which country is your best customer in today?", "calls": 5, "feel": "Will you understand my market?", "id": "intl", "n": 5, "q": "Do you work in other countries and languages?", "theme": "How it works", "tricks": ["Say yes plainly", "Start with the best market", "Ask where customers are now"], "why": "Say yes, then give a calm strategy: start with the best market."}, {"a": "No revenue share, only management fees. No free work and no splitting payment. Occasional performance deals have been done where sales are provable, but the price stays the same. Monthly billing means they are never paying three months up front.", "aiBetter": "We do not do revenue share, it gets messy to track. What keeps you safe is the 10 day exit and billing one month at a time. If it is not working, you stop. That is the same protection without the complicated math.", "better": "We do not do revenue share. It gets messy to track. What keeps you safe is the 10 day exit and billing one month at a time. If it is not working, you stop. That is the same protection, without the complicated math.", "calls": 5, "feel": "Can we share the risk?", "id": "perf", "n": 5, "q": "Can you work on performance, revenue share or a free trial?", "theme": "Pricing and budget", "tricks": ["Do not work for free", "Offer the exit as the safety net", "Keep billing monthly"], "why": "Redirect from risk to the exit. They want safety, not free work."}, {"a": "Flat retainers, no revenue share. In one case he offered about $1,000 for each Google Ads client referred. He is fine working beside other agencies on different channels.", "aiBetter": "I like how you are thinking. We keep a flat retainer so everything stays simple and fair, but I love working with partners. If you bring a client, I will thank you properly, and we can work next to your team without getting in the way. Tell me how you picture it working and we will find the version that is good for both of us.", "better": "I like how you think. We keep a flat monthly fee so things stay simple and fair. But I like working with partners. If you bring us a client, I will thank you properly, and we can work alongside your team. Tell me how you picture it, and we can find a version that works for both of us.", "calls": 3, "feel": "Is there something in this for both of us?", "id": "partner", "n": 4, "q": "Can we partner, split work or do a referral deal?", "theme": "Pricing and budget", "tricks": ["Say yes to the relationship", "Hold the price structure", "Invite them to shape it"], "why": "Be warm, hold the structure, and invite them to design the details with you."}, {"a": "They are used to restricted brands. As a Google partner they use long tail keywords as a workaround, check copy with AI, and keep an approval sheet so the client can accept or reject ads.", "aiBetter": "That is a stressful spot, and you are not the first. We work with restricted brands often. We study what the platforms allow before writing a single ad, use safer long tail keywords, and keep a shared sheet where you approve every ad first. And you stay in control of your own account, so nothing hides from you. What happened the last time your ad was flagged?", "better": "That is a stressful spot, and you are not the first. We work with restricted brands often. We check what the platforms allow before writing a single ad, use safer, longer keyword phrases, and keep a shared sheet where you approve every ad first. You stay in control of your own account. What happened the last time an ad got flagged?", "calls": 4, "feel": "I have been banned or flagged before and I am afraid of it happening again.", "id": "restricted", "n": 4, "q": "Can you advertise my restricted or regulated product?", "theme": "Services and fit", "tricks": ["Normalize the problem", "Show the safety process", "Let them tell the story"], "why": "Empathy first, then a clear process that shows control, and a question that lets them tell the story."}, {"a": "Leads can flow almost anywhere with Zapier or Make. They do not work inside CRMs or answer phones, and fast follow up is the client's job.", "aiBetter": "Good thinking, because a lead is only worth something if someone calls it back fast. We send every lead straight into your CRM through Zapier, so nothing gets lost. The follow up is on your side, and the faster you call, the better the ads look, so I would aim for within five minutes. What do you use today?", "better": "Yes. We send every lead straight into your CRM through Zapier, so nothing gets lost. Then your team does the follow up. The faster you call back, the better the ads look, so aim for within five minutes. What CRM do you use today?", "calls": 3, "feel": "I do not want good leads to slip through the cracks.", "id": "crm", "n": 4, "q": "Can leads go into my CRM, and who follows up?", "theme": "How it works", "tricks": ["Name the fear before the tool", "Give one simple rule (call in five minutes)", "Ask what they use today"], "why": "Answer the real fear (lost leads), then hand over one simple rule they can act on."}, {"a": "Luke agreed that training an internal team can be a good option, but said it takes time and doing it well is hard.", "aiBetter": "That is a smart question, and doing it yourself can work. Here is the honest trade: you save the fee but you spend the learning time, usually a few months and some wasted ad spend. If time is tight I would hire us for three months and have us teach you as we go. What matters more to you right now, saving cash or saving time?", "better": "Doing it yourself can work. The honest trade is this: you save the fee, but you spend the learning time, usually a few months and some wasted ad spend. If time is tight, I would hire us for three months and we teach your team as we go. What matters more right now, saving cash or saving time?", "calls": 3, "feel": "Am I wasting money by hiring someone?", "id": "diy", "n": 3, "q": "Should I try it myself first or train my own team?", "theme": "Services and fit", "tricks": ["Validate their idea", "Name the real trade off", "Ask what matters most"], "why": "Respect their option, show the real trade off, and let them choose."}, {"a": "", "ai": true, "aiBetter": "ReachGiant helps customers find you and choose you. We run Google Ads, Facebook and Instagram ads, and SEO. We also do AI search, so you show up when people ask ChatGPT or Perplexity. And we build your brand and your website, so people land on you, trust you, and buy.", "better": "ReachGiant helps customers find you and choose you. We run Google Ads, Facebook and Instagram ads, and SEO. We also do AI search, so you show up when people ask ChatGPT or Perplexity. And we build your brand and your website, so people land on you, trust you, and buy.", "calls": 0, "feel": "", "id": "ai-what", "n": 0, "q": "What does ReachGiant do?", "theme": "Services and fit", "tricks": [], "why": ""}, {"a": "", "ai": true, "aiBetter": "Google Ads, Meta ads, SEO, AI search, branding, and web development. Most people start with one thing that fits, then add more once it is working.", "better": "Google Ads, Meta ads, SEO, AI search, branding, and web development. Most people start with one thing that fits, then add more once it is working.", "calls": 0, "feel": "", "id": "ai-services", "n": 0, "q": "What services do you offer?", "theme": "Services and fit", "tricks": [], "why": ""}, {"a": "", "ai": true, "aiBetter": "We are an incredible team, and we do excellent work. Our reputation speaks for itself.", "better": "We are an incredible team, and we do excellent work. Our reputation speaks for itself.", "calls": 0, "feel": "", "id": "ai-choose", "n": 0, "q": "Why should I choose you?", "theme": "Proof and experience", "tricks": [], "why": ""}, {"a": "", "ai": true, "aiBetter": "We cater to you. We communicate over email, Zoom, and Loom videos, and whatever you need, we do. Communication is our biggest strength.", "better": "We cater to you. We communicate over email, Zoom, and Loom videos, and whatever you need, we do. Communication is our biggest strength.", "calls": 0, "feel": "", "id": "ai-talk", "n": 0, "q": "How do you communicate?", "theme": "How it works", "tricks": [], "why": ""}, {"a": "", "ai": true, "aiBetter": "Everything is on our pricing page at reachgiant.com/pricing. Take a look, and I can walk you through what fits your goals.", "better": "Everything is on our pricing page at reachgiant.com/pricing. Take a look, and I can walk you through what fits your goals.", "calls": 0, "feel": "", "id": "ai-cost", "n": 0, "q": "How much does it cost?", "theme": "Pricing and budget", "tricks": [], "why": ""}, {"a": "", "ai": true, "aiBetter": "Setup takes about 7 days. Once you say yes, we get everything ready in that time, and you see the full plan before anything goes live.", "better": "Setup takes about 7 days. Once you say yes, we get everything ready in that time, and you see the full plan before anything goes live.", "calls": 0, "feel": "", "id": "ai-long", "n": 0, "q": "How long does it take?", "theme": "Results and timeline", "tricks": [], "why": ""}, {"a": "", "ai": true, "aiBetter": "It is three simple steps. First, I send you a payment link. Second, you fill in a short onboarding form, about 15 minutes. Third, Matthew calls you and we get started. You can start with one channel and add more later.", "better": "It is three simple steps. First, I send you a payment link. Second, you fill in a short onboarding form, about 15 minutes. Third, Matthew calls you and we get started. You can start with one channel and add more later.", "calls": 0, "feel": "", "id": "ai-forward", "n": 0, "q": "How do I move forward?", "theme": "How it works", "tricks": [], "why": ""}, {"a": "", "ai": true, "aiBetter": "No. It is a three month minimum, billed one month at a time. If it is not right for you, you can leave with 10 days notice. The ad accounts stay in your name the whole time.", "better": "No. It is a three month minimum, billed one month at a time. If it is not right for you, you can leave with 10 days notice. The ad accounts stay in your name the whole time.", "calls": 0, "feel": "", "id": "ai-contract", "n": 0, "q": "Is there a long contract?", "theme": "Contracts and commitment", "tricks": [], "why": ""}, {"a": "", "ai": true, "aiBetter": "No, and I will not promise a number, because anyone who does is guessing. What I can promise is daily work and full honesty. If something is not working after about two weeks, I will tell you straight and change the plan.", "better": "No, and I will not promise a number, because anyone who does is guessing. What I can promise is daily work and full honesty. If something is not working after about two weeks, I will tell you straight and change the plan.", "calls": 0, "feel": "", "id": "ai-guarantee", "n": 0, "q": "Can you guarantee results?", "theme": "Results and timeline", "tricks": [], "why": ""}, {"a": "", "ai": true, "aiBetter": "You get a team. Matthew Overbay leads it. Behind him are Google and Meta specialists, a designer for the ads, and a developer who sets up the tracking, so the work is never on one person.", "better": "You get a team. Matthew Overbay leads it. Behind him are Google and Meta specialists, a designer for the ads, and a developer who sets up the tracking, so the work is never on one person.", "calls": 0, "feel": "", "id": "ai-team", "n": 0, "q": "Who will actually work on my account?", "theme": "Who does the work", "tricks": [], "why": ""}]}$json$::jsonb, updated_at = now()
